  "content": {
    "text": "CONCLUDED\n1 day ago\nApple won't be able to roll out its new AI features in all markets right away\nApple finally is getting closer to rolling out a smarter version of Siri — but there will be regional limitations at the outset.\nFor example, the new Siri won't be available right away in the E.U. due to restrictions in the region. \"We're working hard to find a path forward,\" Craig Federighi, the company's senior vice president of software engineering, said during the keynote.\nApple won't be able to immediately roll out the new Siri in China either.",
